{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation\nA gating run in one session was killed by low memory (not a test failure). Investigation found three worktrees concurrently running full pytest-xdist suites (bug-lowcost-git-subprocess-timeout, fix-crane-fixture, plus the reporting session). Three concurrent suites on one host exhausted memory. Confirmed environmental cause: host memory contention, remedy applied was halving workers; fallback is serial. This is the same failure class as the 2026-09-06 host memory-exhaustion incident.\n\n## Problem\nmake verify / make test default to PYTEST_WORKERS=4 (often raised to 8) per invocation, with no cross-session coordination. N parallel agent sessions => N*workers pytest processes, unbounded aggregate memory. Each agent behaves correctly locally; the host-level aggregate is the defect. Also noted: pgrep -f pytest matches ALL sessions' workers (text is not identity), so naive post-kill sweeps would kill other sessions' work — cleanup guidance must stay worktree-scoped.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A mechanism bounds aggregate test-suite resource use across concurrent sessions on one host (e.g. cooperative host-wide concurrency cap for full-suite runs, worker autoscaling from available memory, or documented+enforced stagger protocol). Mechanism-ratchet: justify any new lock/env_var with a mechanism-ok marker referencing this ticket.\n- [x] Solution preserves parallel multi-agent development (serializing all verifies outright is unacceptable friction).\n- [x] A killed-by-OOM run is distinguishable from a test failure in guidance/output so agents apply the environmental-fault remedy instead of retrying blind or root-causing a phantom flake.\n- [x] AGENTS.md/docs updated: worktree-scoped process cleanup only (never pgrep -f pytest sweeps); reduced-worker/serial fallback protocol on memory kill.\n- [x] Regression evidence for the chosen mechanism."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788948835952593001,"uuid":"635d9aad-b6f9-4e83-b5cc-3b8e1bc832a6"}